Description: tests: join the TestWindowThread watchdog before tearing down
 The watchdog was a nux::SystemThread that the fixture deleted in its
 destructor. It writes to the quit pipe and then returns through
 SystemThread::Run, which still uses the object (parent_, SetThreadState,
 TerminateChildThreads). The write wakes the main loop, the test ends, and
 when the fixture is faster the thread runs on freed memory: SIGSEGV in
 SystemThread::Run (SystemThread.cpp:91) while the main thread is already in
 ~GraphicsDisplay. NThread's destructor only detaches, and it detaches even a
 joined thread, so the object cannot be joined and then deleted either.
 .
 Use a std::thread for the watchdog and join it in the destructor. On target2,
 TestWindowThread.* crashed in 5 of 20 runs before and 0 of 30 after.
Author: NeiroNext <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
